  "limitations": [
    "cancelAppointment was excluded from scope, so its checks are untested.",
    "Schemathesis ran in safe mode (GET, HEAD and OPTIONS) while the stdlib sender was allowed writes; createAppointment was exercised only by stdlib cases, and no stateful sequences ran (the contract has no links).",
    "dailyReport's Report schema uses dependentRequired, which the stdlib checker can't evaluate; its bodies were checked against the other keywords only (schema_conformance is cantTell, contract issue C2).",
    "oasdiff is not installed: the breaking-change diff is the stdlib one only.",
    "The stdlib generator can't synthesise strings from a pattern; random createAppointment bodies reuse the documented time.",
    "Random path ids were drawn from 1-1000, so most getClinician and getAppointment samples hit 404s; the specialty failure on getClinician was found by Schemathesis and reproduced with an added case.",
    "F10 is intermittent: 2 of 17 listSlots requests, neither repeated. Its rate is unknown.",
    "One seed (1611) and at most 50 cases per operation: other inputs may fail in ways this run did not see."
  ],
  "next_steps": [
    "Fix F1 first: add the bearer check to /reports/daily and rerun auth_enforced.",
    "Decide F2 and F6 with the client teams: both change what generated clients see.",
    "Before releasing 1.5.0, review the 10 breaking changes against 1.4.0 (B1-B10): bump the major version or restore the removed room property, the 404 response and the optional clinic_id.",
    "Rerun with a second seed and Schemathesis with writes allowed on a disposable instance, to cover createAppointment."
  ]
